{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TKG8HBvo8GRY5ixzoUXuPf","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/source/progress.rst:99:Transient progress\ndocs/source/progress.rst:102:Normally when you exit the progress context manager (or call :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.stop`) the last refreshed display remains in the terminal with the cursor on the following line. You can also make the progress display disappear on exit by setting ``transient=True`` on the Progress constructor. Here's an example::\ndocs/source/progress.rst:104:    with Progress(transient=True) as progress:\ndocs/source/progress.rst:108:Transient progress displays are useful if you want more minimal output in the terminal when tasks are complete.\ndocs/source/progress.rst:280:        for letter in track(\"ABCDEF\", transient=True):\ndocs/source/console.rst:404:If Rich detects that it is not writing to a terminal it will strip control codes from the output. If you want to write control codes to a regular file then set ``force_terminal=True`` on the constructor.\ndocs/source/conf.py:68:# so a file named \"default.css\" will overwrite the builtin \"default.css\".\ndocs/source/live.rst:79:Transient display\ndocs/source/live.rst:83:You can also make the live display disappear on exit by setting ``transient=True`` on the Live constructor.\ndocs/source/live.rst:106:    Once the live display stops on a non-transient renderable, the last frame will render as **visible** since it doesn't have to be cleared."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cfdd711-c25c-4da0-8e66-2bd1f1734728","uuid":"60a41bd7-aab5-40b4-870a-b4780e7e7b67","timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:57:50.555Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"docs/source/progress.rst:99:Transient progress\ndocs/source/progress.rst:102:Normally when you exit the progress context manager (or call :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.stop`) the last refreshed display remains in the terminal with the cursor on the following line. You can also make the progress display disappear on exit by setting ``transient=True`` on the Progress constructor. Here's an example::\ndocs/source/progress.rst:104:    with Progress(transient=True) as progress:\ndocs/source/progress.rst:108:Transient progress displays are useful if you want more minimal output in the terminal when tasks are complete.\ndocs/source/progress.rst:280:        for letter in track(\"ABCDEF\", transient=True):\ndocs/source/console.rst:404:If Rich detects that it is not writing to a terminal it will strip control codes from the output. If you want to write control codes to a regular file then set ``force_terminal=True`` on the constructor.\ndocs/source/conf.py:68:# so a file named \"default.css\" will overwrite the builtin \"default.css\".\ndocs/source/live.rst:79:Transient display\ndocs/source/live.rst:83:You can also make the live display disappear on exit by setting ``transient=True`` on the Live constructor.\ndocs/source/live.rst:106:    Once the live display stops on a non-transient renderable, the last frame will render as **visible** since it doesn't have to be cleared.","numLines":10,"totalLines":10},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TKG8HBvo8GRY5ixzoUXuPf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
